
"smart_sources:2026-05-08 - _Mom, I hope we can afford my school_ -Idaho’s school choice critics ignore the children being helped.md": {"path":"2026-05-08 - _Mom, I hope we can afford my school_ -Idaho’s school choice critics ignore the children being helped.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"12ff7lg","at":1785795032680},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783544316083,"size":7431,"at":1785795032775,"hash":"12ff7lg"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,74]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Chris Cargill","target":"Chris Cargill","line":5},{"title":"Recent coverage has repeatedly referred to the program as a “voucher” despite the fact that it is a tax credit program.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/opinion/article315672266.html?link_source=ta_first_comment&taid=69fdcb9b2ac13600010c49bc&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=social&utm_source=facebook&fbclid=IwY2xjawRrG_ZleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFxSldhSTI2cTlsejRNenVFc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHra27lP2dTCa9DHdTz7NX9KNfoTs-wGRYotI6bSd8sxrQjioUQwUNIPRVB_2_aem_19sezT_gOLlzE_DOZWwv_A","line":18},{"title":"Smiling boy in a yellow shirt against a neutral background, conveying a cheerful and warm mood.","target":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/11062b_d0e9b1c178a74d37a54686b50bd2c469~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_350,h_238,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/11062b_d0e9b1c178a74d37a54686b50bd2c469~mv2.jpg","line":20,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"\"Mom, I hope we can afford my school\" -Idaho’s school choice critics ignore the children being helped","source":"https://www.mountainstatespolicy.org/post/mom-i-hope-we-can-afford-my-school-idaho-s-school-choice-critics-ignore-the-children-being-helpe?utm_campaign=8eaf0750-ca85-4f7b-b48d-c6656bfdc64d&utm_source=so&utm_medium=mail&cid=b0b2ef66-b6e5-475a-a23a-fa59cbad94b8","author":["[[Chris Cargill]]"],"published":"2026-05-08","created":"2026-07-08","description":"We currently know that roughly half of participating families fall below the program’s priority threshold of 300% of the federal poverty level. What we do not know is the median income of all participating families. But critics routinely leap from “we don’t yet know” to “wealthy families are exploiting the system.”"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},